    "manual_confirmation_required": true,
    "manual_confirmation_rule": "For manual acquisition, after attaching the verified report to the matching Zotero item, the user confirms that exact item and attachment in the acquisition queue; the executor then resumes unfinished retrieval work in the same stage without bypassing its review gate. A uniquely matched automatic retrieval does not require this manual action.",
    "fact_classification_rule": "Record retrieval_status, full_text_review_status, and each report-level fact_status separately. Before a report is retrieved or a manual attachment is confirmed, use not_assessed_pending_full_text and not_started. After retrieval but before completed independent review and adjudication, use pending_full_text_review. Use not_reported_in_reviewed_report only for a retrieved report with documented section/page coverage after completed review and adjudication; this does not establish that the outcome was not measured, that there were zero events, or that the value is zero. Use study-level not_reported_after_all_linked_sources_review only when every report in the approved study_report_map has been retrieved, confirmed, independently reviewed, adjudicated, and documented in linked_source_review_evidence. Use cannot_tell_after_full_text_review for an assessed but unresolved reporting question and give an uncertainty_reason. Retrieval failure, inaccessible text, OCR failure, or an unconfirmed manual attachment never establishes factual absence.",
